From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: twobip <github@twobip.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:38:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: keep a DP2HDMI connect when no link
 configuration arrives

A DP2HDMI output asserts its own HPD in dcp_enable_dp2hdmi_hpd(), and its
firmware does not send the link-configuration notification that
dcp_dptx_connect() waits for, so on that path the wait can only time out
and the display is withdrawn before it is ever lit. Continue as the
late-HPD case already does instead of failing the connect. The existing
`compact` case tolerates the same timeout, but it covers the 26.x
firmware's compact endpoints, not a 13.x DP2HDMI output.

Seen on a Mac mini (t8112, G14, DP2HDMI out): the DCP boots, reports
"DP2HDMI HPD connected:1" and 32 modes, then

  dcp_dptx_connect: timed out waiting for port 0 link configuration
  display HPD removed ... set_device_enabled_gated: requested state: 0

and the machine registers a DRM device with no output. With this change the
same machine sets the mode and stays up:

  set_digital_out_mode(...) "3440x1440": 100 ... 3440 ... 1440 ...
  set_digital_out_mode finished:7866

Tested on that machine only (M2 mini, t8112, firmware-compat 13.x); the
T6030/T8122/H17P paths and the compact 26.x path are untouched, and
dcp_is_typec_output() keeps Type-C connects where they are.

Signed-off-by: twobip <github@twobip.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
index a077112f2c..22c3718764 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
@@ -2103,6 +2103,14 @@ static int dcp_dptx_connect_raw(struct apple_dcp *dcp, u32 port, bool *retryable
 	/* T8122 dcpext: HPD only after the link wait, see dcp_ext_dptx_607() */
 	bool late_hpd = dcp_ext_dptx_607(dcp);
 	bool t8132 = dcp_is_t8132_ext(dcp);
+	/*
+	 * A DP2HDMI output asserts its own HPD, in dcp_enable_dp2hdmi_hpd(), and
+	 * that firmware never sends the link-configuration notification the wait
+	 * below looks for, so on this path the wait can only time out. Treat it as
+	 * non-fatal, as the late-HPD and compact cases do, instead of withdrawing
+	 * the display.
+	 */
+	bool dp2hdmi = dcp->hdmi_hpd && !dcp_is_typec_output(dcp);
 	bool compact;
 	unsigned long timeout;
 	u64 generation;
@@ -2267,7 +2275,7 @@ static int dcp_dptx_connect_raw(struct apple_dcp *dcp, u32 port, bool *retryable
 		dev_dbg(dcp->dev,
 			"dcp_dptx_connect: no link configuration on port %u yet\n", port);
 		ret = 0;
-	} else if (!ret && late_hpd) {
+	} else if (!ret && (late_hpd || dp2hdmi)) {
 		/* Without HPD this firmware does not train: assert it now. */
 		dev_dbg(dcp->dev,
 			"dcp_dptx_connect: no link configuration on port %u yet, asserting HPD\n",
-- 
